ublicans on air nearly two-to-one", "Late GOP engagement, including a Trump rally and $2.9 million in outside support for Marques, targets the turnout gap"], "rationale": "The district's seven-point Republican lean, a strong and recently R-tilting expert consensus, and market odds near three in ten for Figures outweigh his clear fundraising and advertising advantages. With all polls stale and partisan-sponsored, the race sits a few points Republican rather than further right.", "watch": "Fresh independent polling or the size of the GOP turnout boost from the Trump rally could push this toward Likely R or back to a true tossup.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Newest usable poll is 46 days old; polling uncertainty inflated.", "Incumbent Shomari Figures (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Alabama's 2nd District pairs a Republican-leaning electorate with a Democratic incumbent, making it one of the cycle's most competitive House races. Shomari Figures enters the fall with a clear money advantage: nearly $1.4 million on hand, a third-quarter fundraising haul roughly three times Rhett Marques's, and Democratic advertisers outspending Republicans almost two-to-one on the air.\n\nRepublicans counter with structural strength: the district leans seven points their way, most expert raters call the race Lean or Likely Republican, and prediction markets price Figures's win odds near three in ten. The only public polls, all Democratic-sponsored and collected by late summer, showed the contest tied within a point. A late Trump rally aimed at boosting GOP turnout underscores that mobilization is the decisive variable in a race expected to stay close but tilt Republican.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.2955, "margin": -3.05}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.2762, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.3161, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.3129, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.2478, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-